<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-power-series" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Power Series</title>
  
  <!-- <introduction>
  <p>
  This is the introduction to the section. It can contain any content
  that is valid in a <introduction> element, including <p>, <ul>, <ol>,
  <figure>, and <table>. You can also include other files using
  <xi:include> tags.
  </p>
  </introduction> -->
  
  <subsection>
    <title>Interval of Convergence of Power Series Summary</title>
    <p>
      To determine the interval of convergence of a power series:
    </p>
    <p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <p>
            <alert>Determine the open interval where the series converges</alert>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Use the ratio test (or root test).
          </p>
          <p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Ratio test: <m>L = \lim_{n \to \infty} \abs{\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}} \quad \rightarrow</m> converges if <m>L \lt 1</m>.
              </li>
              <li>
                Root test: <m>L = \lim_{n \to \infty} \sqrt[n]{\abs{a_n}} \quad \rightarrow</m> converges if <m>L \lt 1</m>.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </p>
          <p>
            Solve the resulting inequality to find the (open) interval where the series converges, which will always be of the form <m>(a - R, a + R)</m>, where <m>R</m> is the radius of convergence.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            <alert>Test the endpoints separately</alert>. Check the convergence of the series at <m>x = a - R</m> and <m>x = a + R</m> by substituting these values into the original series, and using a suitable test or the convergence or divergence of a known series. Some common series forms you'll see:
          </p>
          <p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Harmonic series
              </li>
              <li>
                Alternating harmonic series
              </li>
              <li>
                Divergence test (terms don't approach 0)
              </li>
              <li>
                <m>p</m>-series
              </li>
              <li>
                Alternating series test (alternating series whose terms approach 0)
              </li>
            </ul>
          </p>
          <p>
            (If <m>R = \infty</m> or <m>R = 0</m>, there are no endpoints to test)
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            <alert>Form the complete interval of convergence</alert>, by combining the interval from step 2 and the endpoints from step 3.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </p>
    <p>
      Remarks:
    </p>
    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Often, when testing the endpoints, the two values of <m>x</m> will lead to a very similar series. Contrasting where they are different can help you think about which converges and/or which diverges.
        </li>
        <li>
          The ratio test is used for about 90% of all examples. However, sometimes both can be used, and the root test uses easier algebra, particularly when there are a lot of exponents of <m>n</m>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Note that with the ratio test (or root test), the limit is with respect to <m>n</m>, and so <m>x</m> is a constant with respect to the limit.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </p>
  </subsection>
  
  <subsection>
    <title>Examples</title>
    <exercise>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the interval of convergence and radius of convergence of each series.
        </p>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{3(x+1)^n}{n \cdot 4^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(x-3)^n}{n^2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} n! (2x + 1)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} (-1)^n n x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \sqrt{n} \, x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^n}{\sqrt[3]{n}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n}{5^n} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{5^n}{n} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{n 3^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n}{n+1} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{2n-1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^n}{n^2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} n^n x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{n 4^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} 2^n n^2 x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n 4^n}{\sqrt{n}} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n-1}}{n 5^n} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n}{2^n (n^2+1)} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^{2n}}{n!}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(x-2)^n}{n^2+1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n}{(2n-1) 2^n} (x-1)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1 + n}{n^3 2^n} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(x + 1)^n}{n 2^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} n! x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(x-1)^n}{n^3 \cdot 3^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{\sqrt{n} \cdot (x+6)^n}{8^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{2}{3^n (x-1)^{n+1}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(4x+5)^n}{n^2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{(x+2)^n}{2^n \ln n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(x-2)^n}{n^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=4}^{\infty} \frac{\ln n}{n} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n}{n \ln n} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} n!(2x-1)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(5x-4)^n}{n^3}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{x^{2n}}{n (\ln n)^2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (x+5)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (-1)^n(4x+1)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(3x-2)^n}{n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(x-2)^n}{10^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (2x)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{n x^n}{n+2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n(x+2)^n}{n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{n\sqrt{n}\,3^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(x-1)^n}{\sqrt{n}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^n}{n!}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{3^n x^n}{n!}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{4^n x^{2n}}{n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{\sqrt{n^2+3}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^{n+1}}{\sqrt{n}+3}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{n(x+3)^n}{5^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{n x^n}{4^n (n^2+1)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{\sqrt{n}\,x^n}{3^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \sqrt[n]{n}\,(2x+5)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \bigl(2+(-1)^n\bigr)\,(x+1)^{n-1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n 3^{2n}(x-2)^n}{3n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \left(1+\frac{1}{n}\right)^n x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} (\ln n)\,x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} n! (x-4)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1}(x+2)^n}{n\,2^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (-2)^n (n+1) (x-1)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \left(\frac{x}{4}\right)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^n}{n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (-1)^{n+1} (n+1)x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{5^n}{n!}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(3x)^n}{(2n)!}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (2n)! \left(\frac{x}{3}\right)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^n}{(n+1)(n+2)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1} x^n}{6^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n n! (x-5)^n}{3^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1}(x-4)^n}{n 9^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(x-3)^{n+1}}{(n+1)4^{n+1}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1}(x-1)^{n+1}}{n+1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1}(x-2)^n}{n 2^n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(x-3)^{n-1}}{3^{n-1}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n x^{2n+1}}{2n+1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n}{n+1} (-2x)^{n-1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{x^{3n+1}}{(3n+1)!}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n! x^n}{(2n)!}</m></li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
  </subsection>
  
  <subsection>
    <title>Advanced Examples</title>
    <exercise>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the interval of convergence and radius of convergence of each series.
        </p>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(x-2)^n}{n^{4/5} (5^n - 4)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n}{b^n} (x - a)^n \quad (b\gt 0)</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(2x-1)^n}{5^n \sqrt{n}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{b^n} (x-a)^n</m> (where <m>b \gt 0</m>)</li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{b^n}{\ln n} (x-a)^n</m> (where <m>b \gt 0</m>)</li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n^2 x^n}{2 \cdot 4 \cdot 6 \cdots (2n)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{1 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 \cdots (2n-1)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n! x^n}{1 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 \cdots (2n-1)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{n(\ln n)^2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{n \ln n}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(4x-5)^{2n+1}}{n^{3/2}}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(3x+1)^{n+1}}{2n+2}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{2\cdot 4 \cdot 6 \cdots (2n)}\,x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{3\cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdots (2n+1)}{n^2\,2^n}\,x^{n+1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{2 \cdot 3 \cdot 4 \cdots (n+1)}{n!} x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \left(\frac{2 \cdot 4 \cdot 6 \cdots (2n)}{3 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdots (2n+1)}\right) x^{2n+1}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1} 3 \cdot 7 \cdot 11 \cdots (4n-1)}{4^n} (x-3)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n! (x+1)^n}{1 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 \cdots (2n-1)}</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1+2+3+\cdots+n}{1^2+2^2+3^2+\cdots+n^2}\,x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \bigl(\sqrt{n+1}-\sqrt{n}\bigr)\,(x-3)^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(n!)^k}{(kn)!} x^n</m> (where <m>k</m> is a positive integer)</li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the radius of convergence of each power series.
        </p>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \brac{\frac{2 \cdot 4 \cdot 6 \cdots (2n)}{2 \cdot 5 \cdot 8 \cdots (3n-1)}}^2 x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n!}{3 \cdot 6 \cdot 9 \cdots 3n} \, x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(n!)^2}{2^n (2n)!} \, x^n</m></li>
            <li><m>\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \brac{\frac{n}{n+1}}^{n^2} x^n</m></li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the interval of convergence and radius of convergence of each series. Then, find the sum of the series for <m>x</m> in that interval.
        </p>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <m>\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(x+1)^{2n}}{9^n}</m>.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <hint>
        <p>
          The series is geometric.
        </p>
      </hint>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>(-4,2)</m>, converges to <m>\frac{9}{8-x^2-2x}</m>.
        </p>
      </answer>
    </exercise>
  </subsection>
</section>